"Another variable you can use in your kernel recipe append file is the "
":term:`FILESEXTRAPATHS` variable. When you use this statement, you are "
"extending the locations used by the OpenEmbedded system to look for files"
" and patches as the recipe is processed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../kernel-dev/common.rst:464
msgid ""
"There are other ways of grouping and defining configuration options. For "
"example, if you are working with a local clone of the kernel repository, "
"you could checkout the kernel's ``meta`` branch, make your changes, and "
"then push the changes to the local bare clone of the kernel. The result "
"is that you directly add configuration options to the ``meta`` branch for"
" your BSP. The configuration options will likely end up in that location "
"anyway if the BSP gets added to the Yocto Project."
